   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1943-01-05">Jauary 5, 1943.</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor Paul Tillich</rs><lb/>
               Union Theological Seminary<lb/> Broadway &amp; 120 Street<lb/>
               <rs ref="#" type="place">New York, N.Y.</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>Referring to the telephone conversation your secretary had with our <rs ref="#"
               type="person">Mr. Nathan</rs><!-- unklar wer gemeint ist, vielleicht Robert R. Nathan --> today, I would like to advise you that Special
               Events broadcasts customarily are not paid for. They are considered a contribution to
               the war effort.</p>
            <p>There is, however, a possibility to compensate the speaker for expenses which he had
               in order to prepare and record the talk. These expenses are being repaid on request
               only. The approved rates vary from $5.- to $12.-.</p>
            <p>We have requested your compensation from our agency, Short-Wave Research, but we must
               ask you to register at Short-Wave Research, 730 Fifth Avenue, Room 1106. You can
               register there at any time at your convenience. After you registered, the check will
               be mailed to you within a period from several weeks to approximately two month.</p>
            
            <closer>
               <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__683" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Lewis F. Gittler</hi> <lb/>Lewis F. Gittler</rs><lb/>Acting Chief<lb/>
               Special Events Department</signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
